<h1>About</h1>
<figure class="float-right about-photo">
    <img src="/assets/me.jpeg" alt="Me at Memorial Terrace in graduation regalia.">
</figure>
<p>
    I'm Nico, a programmer from Wisconsin! In tech, my interests span full-stack development, systems performance, and AI.
    At <a href="https://abbvie.com/" target="_blank">AbbVie</a>, I lead the technical development of applications in clinical R&D, working across application architecture, integrations, and AI orchestration.
    In my free time, I like to draw, <a href="https://app.thestorygraph.com/profile/nicosalm" target="_blank">read (paper) books</a>, and recently started to get into climbing.
    I post monthly updates to my <a href="/now">now page</a>.
</p>

Find me on <a href="https://github.com/nicosalm" target="_blank">GitHub</a>, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicosalm/" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>, <a href="https://x.com/salmdotdev" target="_blank">Twitter</a>, or say hi via {% include "email-link.njk" %}!
<h2 id="studies"><a href="#studies" class="heading-link">Studies</a></h2>
<p>
    In 2026, I graduated from the <a href="/writing/my-wisconsin-experience/">University of Wisconsin-Madison</a> with a B.S. in Computer Sciences and Data Science.
</p>
<p>
<ul><li>I was a member of <a href="https://engineering.wisc.edu/directory/profile/dane-morgan" target="_blank">Dane Morgan's</a> <a href="https://skunkworks.engr.wisc.edu/" target="_blank">Informatics Skunkworks</a> research group for two years,  where I trained generative models to design new crystal structures with target physical properties. I helped found the <a href="https://wqi.wisc.edu/wqcc/" target="_blank">Wisconsin Quantum Computing Club</a>, and later competed with the group at <a href="https://www.iquise.mit.edu/iQuHACK/2024-02-02" target="_blank">MIT's IQuHACK</a>. I was also a regular at the <a href="https://upl.cs.wisc.edu/" target="_blank">Undergraduate Projects Lab</a>, where I served as a lab coordinator, introduced its <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@undergraduateprojectslab" target="_blank">Lightning Talks</a>, and organized <a href="https://www.madhacks.io/" target="_blank">MadHacks</a>, growing the hackathon to a record 417 participants.</li></ul>
</p>
<h2 id="colophon"><a href="#colophon" class="heading-link">Colophon</a></h2>
<p>This site is <a href="/writing/opinions-on-web-design/">built</a> with <a href="https://www.11ty.dev/" target="_blank">Eleventy</a>, HTML, and CSS. I try to keep the JavaScript light, but it leaks into blog posts to render the table of contents, sidenotes, and category filters, as well as MathJax for pages that need it. Images are converted to AVIF at build, and links prefetch on hover via <a href="https://instant.page/" target="_blank">instant.page</a>. There's an <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>, a <a href="/sitemap.xml">sitemap</a>, and a <a href="/status">status page</a>. Source <a href="https://github.com/nicosalm/salm.dev/" target="_blank">on GitHub</a>.</p>

